# Architecture

## Apps

| App | Path | Role |
|-----|------|------|
| Storefront | `apps/storefront` | Next.js customer UI, i18n routes, composes Medusa + Payload data |
| Commerce | `apps/commerce` | Medusa — carts, orders, payments, subscriptions, shipping, product catalog for sale |
| CMS | `apps/cms` | Payload — pages, articles, navigation, homepage, editorial product copy; live preview to storefront |

## Source of truth

- **Prices, inventory, cart, checkout, orders, subscriptions, shipping options:** Medusa only.
- **Marketing copy, SEO text, layout content, nav/footer, homepage sections:** Payload. Reference Medusa entities by ID/handle where needed; do not duplicate commerce state in CMS.
- **Customer-facing URLs:** Storefront (`/da/...`, `/en/...`).

## Cross-app changes

When a feature touches more than one app, state which app owns persistence and which only reads/displays. Avoid implementing the same business rule in both Medusa and Payload.
